        "original_id": "bc5e8808-d2e8-518f-a528-79513c44de89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Right Stuff\n- People: Levon Helm, Jack Ridley, Ed Harris\n- Roles: narrator, Air Force test pilot, aeronautical engineer, chief of the U.S. Air Force's Flight Test Engineering Laboratory\n\nFacts:\n- Jack Ridley was born on June 16, 1915.\n- Jack Ridley was an aeronautical engineer, a USAF test pilot, and chief of the U.S. Air Force's Flight Test Engineering Laboratory.\n- Jack Ridley died on March 12, 1957.\n- The Right Stuff is a 1983 American epic historical drama film.\n- In The Right Stuff, Levon Helm narrated the introduction and other parts of the film and also co-starred as Air Force test pilot Jack Ridley.\n- Ed Harris is known for a performance in The Right Stuff (1983).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
